  "title": "MEG-BIDS OMEGA RestingState_sample",
  "description": "A sample resting-state MEG dataset from the Open MEG Archive (OMEGA), containing 5-minute eyes-open recordings from five subjects. Data were acquired at the Montreal Neurological Institute with a 275-channel CTF MEG system and include head shape digitization and defaced structural T1 images processed with FreeSurfer. The dataset is organized according to the MEG-BIDS specification.",
  "methods_description": "Recordings were made with a CTF 275 MEG system at a 2400 Hz sampling rate with a 600 Hz anti-aliasing low-pass filter. Channels included MEG reference sensors, axial gradiometers, and ECG and EOG bipolar channels. Head shape and fiducial points were digitized with a Polhemus Fastrak device driven by Brainstorm. Structural T1 images were defaced and processed with FreeSurfer 5.3.",
